 ('discrete_morse_function.rs',182,'Complete body read. Finite bitmask complex uses an explicitly augmented convention including empty face zero, requires all subsets, unique entries and at most eight vertices, then checks at most one lower face of no smaller value and one upper coface of no larger value. This is a genuine finite discrete-Morse inequality check with supplied integer function. The test pairing a vertex with the empty face makes the augmented convention explicit; no ordinary unreduced critical-cell count or Morse complex construction is inferred. Positive and violation tests exercise actual inequalities.'),
 ('discrete_morse_complex.rs',126,'Complete body read. Label shell and scalar 2*pairs<=cells census with checked arithmetic. Critical count is the arithmetic remainder, conditional on a genuine disjoint matching; there are no cells, incidence, pairing map, acyclicity, boundary or homotopy-equivalence witnesses. Tests verify count arithmetic and overmatching only. The broad module title does not establish a Morse chain complex.'),
